        "original_id": "56e55f6f-bc54-51f6-830b-6c54d3757560",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Croydon Airport, Gatwick Airport, London, South London, south-east England, Central London, Crawley\n- Systems: ICAO, IATA\n- Topics: Airports, airport replacement, airport traffic ranking\n\nFacts:\n- Croydon Airport, with ICAO code EGCR, was an airport in South London, England.\n- Croydon Airport was the main airport for London before Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport, and Gatwick Airport replaced it.\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, has IATA code LGW and ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is a major international airport in south-east England, 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport is the eighth-busiest airport in Europe.",
